## Suggestions for Improvement
- Add more TypeScript types and interfaces for props, stores, and composables
- Document custom hooks and store modules
- Add unit and integration tests (Vitest/Jest)
- Consider lazy-loading routes/components for performance
- Improve accessibility (ARIA, keyboard navigation)
- Use `.env` files for configuration
- Optimize assets (SVG/image compression)
- Add global error handling
- Expand documentation for contributors

Notes and conventions
- Keep page-level code in `src/views/` and group related pages into feature folders (for example, `src/views/auth/`).
- Put reusable, UI-only components in `src/components/` and organize them by responsibility: `auth/`, `presentation/`, `ui/`, `layout/`, `shared/`.
- Use `composables/` for small, focused hooks (prefixed with `use`) and consider adding an `index.ts` barrel to simplify imports.
- When moving components, add a small `index.ts` barrel (per-folder or root `components/index.ts`) to minimize churn in import paths.
- Keep `src/plugins/` focused on third-party integration and registration only. Business logic belongs in `composables/` or `stores/`.
- Use the `@/` TypeScript path alias (already configured) for clearer absolute imports (for example: `import { useTheme } from '@/composables'`).

Recommended next steps
- Add per-folder `index.ts` barrels for `components/`, `composables/`, and `stores/` to make reorganizing later easier.
- If CI runs on macOS/Linux, ensure file-name casing is consistent (Windows is case-insensitive which can hide issues).